"Created `test_median.py` with `unittest` tests covering all five required cases (plus two extras), and ran them with `python -m unittest test_median.py -v`. **All 7 tests pass.**\n\n```\ntest_does_not_mutate_input (test_median.TestMedian.test_does_not_mutate_input) ... ok\ntest_empty_list_returns_none (test_median.TestMedian.test_empty_list_returns_none) ... ok\ntest_even_length_list (test_median.TestMedian.test_even_length_list) ... ok\ntest_list_with_duplicates (test_median.TestMedian.test_list_with_duplicates) ... ok\ntest_list_with_negative_numbers (test_median.TestMedian.test_list_with_negative_numbers) ... ok\ntest_odd_length_list (test_median.TestMedian.test_odd_length_list) ... ok\ntest_single_element (test_median.TestMedian.test_single_element) ... ok\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\nRan 7 tests in 0.000s\n\nOK\n```\n\nCoverage:\n- **Odd-length** — `median([3, 1, 2])` → `2`\n- **Even-length** — `median([4, 1, 3, 2])` → `2.5`\n- **Empty list** — returns `None` (checked with `assertIsNone`)\n- **Duplicates** — `median([5, 3, 3, 1, 3])` → `3`\n- **Negative numbers** — `median([-5, -1, -3])` → `-3`\n- Extras: single-element list, and verifying the input list isn't mutated"